# Phase 2.1 — PaddleOCR / Vast.ai development endpoint configuration.
#
# Placeholders only. Copy to a gitignored `.env` (never `.env.paddle.example`
# itself) and fill in real values there — this file is committed and must
# never carry one. `ocr.paddle_config.load_paddle_settings()` fails closed
# (`PaddleConfigError`, naming the exact missing variable) when a required
# variable is absent; there is no default host, port or user.
#
# See docs/moneythumb-replacement/PADDLE_VAST_RUNBOOK.md for the full
# lifecycle (check / deploy / start / tunnel-up / status / measure / stop /
# tunnel-down) and docs/moneythumb-replacement/PHASE2_RULINGS.md's Phase 2.1
# section for the authorization these variables exist under.

# Required always. Closed vocabularies, and the ONLY legal pairing:
#   PADDLE_PROVIDER=vast.ai        -> PADDLE_EXECUTION_CLASS=remote_paid
#   PADDLE_PROVIDER=local          -> PADDLE_EXECUTION_CLASS=local_free
PADDLE_PROVIDER=<set in your shell>
PADDLE_EXECUTION_CLASS=<set in your shell>

# Required only when PADDLE_PROVIDER=vast.ai. The SSH endpoint of the
# explicitly authorized Vast.ai development instance. NEVER a real value in
# this tracked file.
PADDLE_VAST_HOST=<set in your shell>
PADDLE_VAST_SSH_PORT=<set in your shell>
PADDLE_VAST_SSH_USER=<set in your shell>

# Required for ANY remote_paid execution. Must equal this exact literal —
# not "1", "true" or "yes". Independent of the visual rung's own
# OCR_REMOTE_OPT_IN (one opt-in never authorizes two paid extractors).
# COMMENTED OUT ON PURPOSE (MINOR-7, PHASE2_P21PADDLE_REVIEW.md): the runbook
# tells an operator to copy this file to a gitignored `.env`, and
# `ocr/config.py`'s dotenv load puts `.env` into every process's environment
# automatically — an uncommented value here would leave the paid-remote
# opt-in permanently on, defeating "set it only in the environment of the
# specific command" (see PADDLE_VAST_RUNBOOK.md). Uncomment it ONLY in a
# shell you are about to run one deliberate remote command in, never in a
# persisted `.env` file.
# PADDLE_REMOTE_OPT_IN=I_ACCEPT_REMOTE_PAID_PADDLE_OCR

# NEVER set in Phase 2.1. Required in addition to the line above before a
# customer-scope document may reach a remote_paid worker. Setting it without
# Gustavo's separate remote-data / privacy / retention ruling is a doctrine
# violation, not a configuration choice.
# PADDLE_REMOTE_CUSTOMER_DATA_OPT_IN=I_AUTHORIZE_CUSTOMER_DOCUMENTS_TO_REMOTE_PADDLE_OCR

# Optional; sensible defaults shown. The worker's own loopback port on the
# host that runs it, and the LOCAL end of the SSH tunnel (deliberately a
# different number by default, so "localhost" in a log always reads as a
# tunnel, never as a locally-running service).
# PADDLE_WORKER_PORT=8765
# PADDLE_TUNNEL_LOCAL_PORT=18765

# Optional. Override the client's worker URL — MUST be a loopback http(s)
# URL (the tunnel's local end) or the client refuses it outright.
# PADDLE_WORKER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18765

# Optional. A per-session bearer token; `tools/paddle_vast.py start`
# generates one automatically into the gitignored .paddle_runtime/ directory
# when this is left unset. Never commit a real value here.
# PADDLE_WORKER_TOKEN=<set in your shell>

# Optional; default shown. Pidfiles, the session token and the tunnel log —
# gitignored.
# PADDLE_RUNTIME_DIR=.paddle_runtime

# Optional connection tuning for a slow link: yes or no. Unset/blank keeps
# the existing SSH configuration. Applied only when opening a new tunnel;
# compression restores identical bytes and does not change OCR/cache identity.
# PADDLE_VAST_SSH_COMPRESSION=yes
